## Chino Lemon Law and Pre-Owned Vehicles

Both new and used cars are covered under the Lemon Car Law in California.

## Dealerships Warranty

In California, most dealers sell vehicles with a dealer warranty, usually valid for 30 days after purchase or until 1,000 miles on the odometer. You may have a claim if your pre-owned vehicle falls within these terms of lemon car law in California.

Your Rights as a Consumer

Used car dealerships must adhere to the lemon car law in California. They are required to cover repair or provide a buyback for your defective car. If the dealership fails to repair the defect, you can recover the cost of the vehicle, incidental costs, and attorney fees from the warrantor.

Know What Buying a Vehicle “As Is” Means

Buying “as is” means you are responsible for any defects and cannot recover damages under the Lemon Car law in California. However, the dealership must display this agreement clearly in the buyer’s guide. If not, you may still be able to file a claim and recover damages.

