## Chino Lemon Law FAQs

## Does My Car Qualify for A Lemon Law Claim?

Your car must have significant defects covered under the original warranty, which may change depending on the manufacturer. It typically is three years from the date of purchase or 36,000 miles, but the court may view your claim more favorably if you filed it within the early 18-month/18,000-mile window.

## Do I Need a Lemon Law Attorney in Chino, CA?

Technically, you can file a claim without one, but it’s in your best interest to hire a lemon law attorney in Chino, CA. A skilled lawyer increases the chances of a successful claim, so we recommend hiring a lawyer as soon as possible.

## Is There a Time Limit to File a Lemon Law Claim?

Yes, there is a time limit for filing a lemon law claim, usually within four years from when you first notice the defect. However, delaying things can only hurt your claim, so file it as quickly as you can.

## Can I Ask for A Replacement Instead of a Buyback?

Under California lemon law, you can request a replacement vehicle instead of a buyback. Your lemon law attorney can help negotiate the best option based on your preferences and circumstances.

## Does The Chino Lemon Law Apply to Private Car Sales?

Generally, NO. Private car sales don’t fall under the lemon car law in California because these deals are made under an “as is” assumption.

## How Long Will My Chino Lemon Law Claim Take to Settle?

We usually try to settle Chino lemon law cases within 30 days, but there are no guarantees. Sometimes, it can take longer to resolve a claim. It all depends on how complex your case is, among other things, which may affect your timeline. You should consult a lemon law attorney in Chino, CA.
